<title>UK: Kexim sets $350 million 10-year Yankee bond.</title>
<headline>Kexim sets $350 million 10-year Yankee bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Export-Import Bank of Korea (Kexim) has issued a $350 million 10-year Yankee bond issue, lead manager Lehman Brothers said.</p>
<p>The bond will be priced later to yield 45 basis points over the February 2004 U.S. Treasury note.</p>
<p>There is a put after seven years.  </p>
<p>Kexim is rated A1 by Moody's and AA-minus by Standard &amp; Poor's. Fees on the deal total 5/8 percent.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
</text>
